</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 781)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>ARRI&#8217;s tool installs itself.</b> Download &#8220;ARRI Reference Tool 1.0.0 (CMD) for macOS&#8221; &#8212; the last item on ARRI&#8217;s page, not the Viewer or the GUI app &#8212; leave the zip in Downloads and drop your clips again: Asobi unpacks it into its own Tools folder, checks every file carries ARRI&#8217;s signature, and clears the browser&#8217;s quarantine flag so macOS lets it run. (ARRI signed the libraries but didn&#8217;t notarize them, which is why a copy unzipped by hand was refused with &#8220;library load disallowed&#8221;.) Locate art-cmd&#8230; now takes the zip too.</li>
<li>Camera raw opened from the Finder, File &#9656; Open or Open Recent gets the same Develop offer as a drop.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
